Third-party data

  data/test_questions.jsonl contains questions and SPARQL queries from

  - LC-QuAD 2.0: Dubey, Banerjee, Abdelkawi and Lehmann, "LC-QuAD 2.0: A Large Dataset for Complex
    Question Answering over Wikidata and DBpedia", ISWC 2019.
    Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
    (as stated on https://huggingface.co/datasets/lc_quad).
  - QALD-10: Usbeck et al., Semantic Web journal (https://github.com/KGQA/QALD_10).
    Licence: MIT, copyright (c) 2022 Longquan Jiang; the licence text is in data/licenses/QALD-10-MIT.txt.

  Both are taken from the versions prepared for the QLever engine by the Chair of Algorithms and Data
  Structures, University of Freiburg (https://ad-publications.cs.uni-freiburg.de/grisp/benchmark/wikidata/).
  Changes: the SPARQL queries are those of the Freiburg versions, which rewrote the original queries to
  run on QLever and on current Wikidata; only test questions are included; 27 LC-QuAD 2.0 questions whose
  original text was unusable are replaced by their first paraphrase (marked "paraphrase" in the field
  question_source).

  data/labels/ and results/executions.jsonl.gz contain data from Wikidata (CC0).
